From: NexsOS1 build compatibility layer
Subject: [backport] libgcrypt: import target-width size type into GRUB header

GRUB's libgcrypt target implementation is compiled through cipher_wrap.h,
which maps size_t to grub_size_t. Direct target modules include the generated
grub/gcrypt/gcrypt.h without that wrapper. On i386-pc this leaves host size_t
in public declarations and conflicts with the target-width implementation and
grub/crypto.h.

The import filter already removes the only ssize_t occurrence before emitting
the GRUB header, so normalize remaining size_t tokens to grub_size_t. Under
GRUB_UTIL, grub_size_t follows the host pointer width; under target builds it
follows the target pointer width.

--- a/util/import_gcrypth.sed
+++ b/util/import_gcrypth.sed
@@ -13,4 +13,5 @@
 /^typedef gpg_error_t gcry_error_t;/ d
 /^typedef gpg_err_code_t gcry_err_code_t;/ d
 /^typedef struct gcry_mpi \*gcry_mpi_t;/ d
+s/size_t/grub_size_t/g
 p
--- a/util/import_gcrypt_inth.sed
+++ b/util/import_gcrypt_inth.sed
@@ -14,4 +14,5 @@
 /^typedef gpg_err_code_t gcry_err_code_t;/ d
 /^typedef struct gcry_mpi \*gcry_mpi_t;/ d
 /^#error  gcrypt.h already included/ d
+s/size_t/grub_size_t/g
 p
